Why: a host switch (document_edit::set_key_edit_after_insert) for the net-zero key edit after an AXSelectedText insert into a document window, so an embedding app whose inserts already mark the document edited can keep ⌘Z undoing the insert itself.

After an AXSelectedText insert into a document window, type_text sends a
space and a backspace so the document registers the change. In TextEdit on
macOS 27 the insert already goes through the text view's edit model: the
document is marked modified without the key edit, and ⌘Z reverts the insert.
The key edit then becomes its own undo step on top, so ⌘Z undoes only the key
edit and the agent's change can no longer be undone. The switch is on by
default (upstream behaviour unchanged); whole-value writes (set_value) always
keep the key edit. Upstreamable as is.

